export anchor SeedPacketStyle:
    number: 85
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Seed packet
    idea: Every project is a vintage seed packet with a small painted vignette and its progress read as germination, while the fortnight sits in a sowing chart of growing stems.
    base: light
    palette:
        cream: #f7f1e1, the page
        packetPaper: #fffbef, packets, panels and the masthead
        sky: #d7e7e6, the sky behind each vignette
        ink: #2b2a22, text and frames
        soilBrown: #5e5440, labels and notes
        chaff: #c9bc9c, grid lines and meter ticks, never text
        tomato: #a8331f, Design packets, the pinked edge, overdue and Behind
        bean: #3d6b2c, Engineering packets, On track, this week stems and the primary button
        carrot: #8f4a0c, Research packets and At risk
        tulip: #8e2f5a, Marketing packets
        mustard: #d9a72b, the avatar and the focus glow, never text
    type:
        Three stacks. Slab uses Rockwell, Roboto Slab, Clarendon, Georgia
        at 700 for the 38px greeting, 34px contents numbers, 30px brand,
        24px section titles and 18px germination figures. Variety names
        use Georgia bold italic at 21px. Body is Georgia at 16px with 1.5
        line height. Labels use Franklin Gothic Medium, Arial Narrow, Arial
        at 700, 11 to 13px caps tracked 0.12 to 0.14em.
    layout:
        A paper masthead with a red pinked top edge holds a round sprout
        badge, the brand with the line Projects grown from seed, a square
        search field, the New project button, a bell and the user. The nav
        is a row of caps cells split by hairlines, the current one black.
        Two framed panels follow, each with an inset hairline frame. The
        left is the back of a packet with the greeting, the date, a
        sowing note with a red diamond saying 4 tasks are overdue, and a
        packet contents grid of four cells with caps headings and slab
        numbers. The right is the sowing chart, two week blocks of seven
        ruled columns where each day is a stem with a pair of leaves grown
        to its count, with day letters on top and counts below. Below, the
        seed rack shows six portrait packets in three columns. Each packet
        has a team colour frame, a coloured band with the number and the
        brand, a painted vignette of sunflower, bean, carrot or tulip,
        then the variety, the italic name, a ten tick germination meter,
        Sprouted and Harvest facts and the status. A garden diary of six
        dated lines sits beside the rack. Below 1000px the columns stack
        and packets go two across, and one across on a phone.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between packets, 32px between panels, a 6px gap inside each packet frame.
    density: Medium. Each packet carries a picture, a meter and two facts.
    corners: Square, 2px at most. The masthead has a pinked edge.
    borders: A 3px team colour frame plus a 1px inner frame on packets. 2px ink on panels with an inset hairline.
    shadows: A flat 4px offset tint behind packets, like card stock on a shelf.
    icons:
        Small painted plant vignettes per team built from simple shapes.
        Status boxes pair the caps word with a check in a circle for On
        track, an exclamation in a diamond for At risk and a cross in a
        square for Behind. Overdue uses the red diamond.
    focus: A 2px dashed ink outline offset 3px with a 6px mustard glow. A focused field fills pale yellow #fdf3d4.
    tone: A gardener's notes, such as Germination, Sprouted, Harvest and Sow these first.
